[b]Every town has a board with the mercenary contracts on offer.[/b]

Which kingdoms would hire you, what they pay and who they are fighting, on one page. No more riding from lord to lord asking for work to find out who pays best.

The board is only a view of vanilla's own offers: the same conditions and the same pay a lord would give you in conversation, and signing or switching uses vanilla's own actions. Nothing new is invented.

[size=5][b]The board[/b][/size]
In any town menu, pick [b]Mercenary Contract Board[/b]. Every kingdom is listed with its banner:
[code]
Battania (Caladog): 90 per influence
Western Empire (Garios): 60 per influence
Aserai (Unqid): not at war                  (greyed)
Sturgia (Raganvad): never heard of you      (greyed)
[/code]
Hover a line for the ruler, the pay, what signing is worth (5 influence = 450 denars) and the kingdom's wars. A greyed line tells you why that kingdom won't hire you right now. Pick one and press Accept.

[size=5][b]Already under contract?[/b][/size]
Your contract is at the top: the kingdom, its pay, the next monthly pay review (and what the rate would be today), the influence still owed to you and its wars. Accepting another contract asks first: [i]"Leave your contract with Vlandia and sign with Battania?"[/i], with what leaving costs (the influence still owed is lost, as in vanilla). Yes switches, No takes you back to the board. Vassals and rulers get no contracts, and the board says so.

[size=5][b]Vanilla's rules, in plain view[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Only kingdoms at war hire mercenaries.
[*]Your clan tier is at least 1, the ruler's relation with you at least -10, you own no settlement, and every war you fight is theirs too.
[*]They must have heard of you (renown), and not be winning on their own (more than 3 times their enemies' strength).
[*]Pay is denars per influence point you earn in their service, 10 to 800, higher when the kingdom is struggling, +15% per clan tier.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/612]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] ([b]optional[/b]): enabled (on), show kingdoms that would not hire you (on), best pay first (on), confirm a first contract (on). Without MCM the mod runs on these defaults.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/612]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional)
[*]No Harmony needed.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] click Mod Manager Download and enable it.
[*][b]Manual:[/b] extract the zip into [i]Mount & Blade II Bannerlord\Modules\[/i], so you get [i]Modules\MercenaryContractBoard\SubModule.xml[/i]. Enable it in the launcher (below MCM if you use it).
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Game v1.4.8, singleplayer. Works with or without War Sails (port towns have the board too).
[*]Safe to add or remove mid-campaign: nothing is saved into your campaign. Your contract is vanilla's.
[*]Towns only. The text is English only for now.
[*]Also on the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3834681925]Steam Workshop[/url] and on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/mercenary-contract-board/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url]. Same files.
[/list]

Bugs or a mod it fights with: tell me in the comments or on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/mercenary-contract-board/issues]GitHub[/url]. Every rule in detail: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/mercenary-contract-board#readme]README[/url].

